# The ffmpeg build used to re-encode the sound banks. Six hundred megabytes of a
# redistributable nobody needs in order to rebuild the mod; the script that uses it is
# the one file worth keeping and it is two directories down.
tools/ffmpeg/

# The arcabuz used to be ignored here, on the grounds that it was an experiment that never became
# a weapon. It is a weapon now. Nothing is ignored here any more, and the reason is worth writing
# down because the file itself was never what was wrong:
#
#   models/item/arcabuz.json             Blockbench, 64x64, eight elements in six groups
#   textures/models/arcabuz.png          64x320 -- the five frames of the fuse burning down
#   textures/models/arcabuz.png.mcmeta   one line, and the only thing that makes frame one lit
#   textures/particle/arcabuz_shot.png   32x160, the muzzle flash in the strip format the
#                                        slash particle already reads
#
# **The problem was that the model pointed at a path the game never reads.** 1.21.1's blocks.json
# builds the atlas from block/ and item/ and nothing else, so a texture under models/ is never
# stitched and the item renders as the missing cube -- which is what the playtest reported, and
# what the client log said in one line. A file being present is not the same as the game looking
# at it, and three separate things in this project have been that exact bug.
#
# The strip now exists TWICE on purpose. textures/models/arcabuz.png is the original, untouched,
# where it was drawn, so the next person can tell which of the two is the artwork. The five frames
# the model actually reads are cut out under textures/item/arcabuz_fuse/, because that is a
# folder the atlas reads.
